From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodrigo Goya <rodrigo.goya@abcellera.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:58:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] clustalw: give fast_nj_tree a full prototype

GCC 15 defaults to C23, where an empty parameter list declares a
function taking no arguments. The block-scope declaration
'void fast_nj_tree();' in nj_tree() therefore conflicts with the call
fast_nj_tree(tree_description, tree) and with the definition below it.
Declare the full prototype instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vmd/plugins/clustalw/src/trees.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vmd/plugins/clustalw/src/trees.c b/vmd/plugins/clustalw/src/trees.c
index f092f54..945f5fc 100644
--- a/vmd/plugins/clustalw/src/trees.c
+++ b/vmd/plugins/clustalw/src/trees.c
@@ -628,7 +628,7 @@ void nj_tree(char **tree_description, FILE *tree)
 #else /* ORIGINAL_NJ_TREE */
 
 void nj_tree(char **tree_description, FILE *tree) {
-	void fast_nj_tree();
+	void fast_nj_tree(char **tree_description, FILE *tree);
  
 	/*fprintf(stderr, "****** call fast_nj_tree() !!!! ******\n");*/
 	fast_nj_tree(tree_description, tree);
